<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Isabel Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isabel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Isabel is one of the largest islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, lying north-west of Guadalcanal. The Spanish explorer Álvaro de Mendaña named it in 1568. Part of the German Solomon Islands, it was transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> under an agreement of 1899, taking effect in 1900, and it now forms Isabel Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-isabel-island.jpg" alt="Santa Isabel Island" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This map's source is here, with the uploader's modifications, and the GMT homepage says that the tools are released u... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SantaIsabelmap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
